  "closed_findings": [
    {
      "id": "P5-05-R1-zero-settle",
      "priority": "P2",
      "status": "closed_by_source_review",
      "original": "Mac act_and_verify copied the polling changed flag directly into effect_observed. The shared wait_settled zero-budget branch returns changed=False even when its immediate after frame differs significantly.",
      "resolution": "Mac effect_observed now combines polling observations with final ROI changed pixels >= shared _MIN_CHANGE_PX of 8. The shared Windows wait function stays equivalent to its baseline AST.",
      "regression_source": "The pure success case uses actual _after and shared wait_settled with settle_ms=0, a real 600-pixel difference and only native acquisition/dispatch boundaries substituted. The real Node fixture adds a zero-settle counter-change assertion."
    }
  ],
  "source_assessment": {
    "cancellation_and_dispatch": "Mac action capture, click-patch preparation and post-action observation use shielded to_thread tasks. The live pending task is retained, and finally either releases immediately after actual completion or registers a completion callback. Native input is dispatched on the event loop after a cancellation checkpoint and require_fresh. Background workers do not post native input. Requested internal evidence saves may complete after cancellation while retaining the gate, and the README states this scope.",
    "freshness_and_failure": "The original capture timestamp is retained. Exact active target/focus, geometry and ten-second observation age are checked before native dispatch. Click points are mapped inside the actual capture and their 1x1 native pixel plus three-pixel padding is recaptured for equality. Native target/hit guards remain in the reused helper. Post-action observation/image failures preserve the posted action_result, with confirmed null and unconfirmed outcome. The 45-second outer action deadline retains the actual worker gate through cleanup.",
    "shared_frame_coordinates": "Screenshot encoding and OCR use the same captured RGB frame. Screenshot origin, scale and scale_y use actual encoded dimensions and logical_bounds. OCR uses source dimensions with independent axes and preserves negative origins. AX is a separate bounded observation of at most 80 nodes. Named window capture checks handle/PID/bounds and reobserves the complete private target including process birth identity. OCR returns at most 200 words with full count/truncation.",
    "optional_backends": "Without requested screenshot pixels, unavailable OCR causes no OCR-only capture. A typed OCR-only capture failure is stored under backend_errors and does not prevent AX results. Explicit screenshot capture failures remain errors. _optional catches ordinary exceptions, preserves typed code/details, and does not catch Python3.12 asyncio.CancelledError. Observe keeps an 80-second outer deadline.",
    "toolset_isolation": "Observation imports utils.macos_ocr, whose imports do not register tools. The shared pure backend retains OCR gating/validation and permits observe-only OCR without loading direct OCR/capture/input modules. The Mac registry maps observe/action verification explicitly and enables batch separately. Native recording remains unsupported. Per-readiness listing and diagnostics distinguish capture observation, guarded action verification and macro replay.",
    "macro_and_images": "Mac-only batch.wait accepts finite nonnegative seconds, caps at300 and awaits cancellable asyncio.sleep. Cancellation propagates out of batch execution before later steps. Macro replay uses the existing live registry and per-tool guard path. Lifted image metadata is read from the actual image container, including nested screenshot dictionaries, so both the top-level image and lifted_images entry retain the correct width/height/scale/scale_y/origin/logical_bounds/coordinate_space/source_pixel_scale.",
    "diagnostics": "Mac optional OCR/AX availability is based on installed native backend support, so observe-only internal use is reported. desktop.observe and desktop.action_verification separate screen and input readiness. desktop.macro_replay can be ready for registry/query/wait sequences without a native helper and reports input readiness separately.",
    "test_and_fixture_updates": "smoke_macos_shared pins an absent helper for host-independent pure readiness checks. Its old macro-unsupported assertion is replaced with implemented batch/macro presence and explicit module mapping, while other unavailable capability checks remain. The App composed mode uses the real LaunchServices App HTTP route and native receiver, with a three-step observe/wait/OCR macro. The native Node composed path uses four action/wait/observe/OCR macro steps and keeps target/focus/no-change/zero-budget/image-coordinate assertions. Other App modes follow their prior branches when composed is false.",
    "documentation": "The composed README and bilingual root README reflect shared observation, pixel verification and macro replay while preserving P5/P5-05 in_progress, future native recording and original environment/signing/Windows gates. Screen changes remain semantically unconfirmed."
  },
